{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnKJ6LZED4djk8BA1fgm", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as the pipeline is concerned, nobody has been told about the $412.30 overspend in the `expand` step.\n\n- **The original nightly run (Nov 4):** it crashed while creating the findings directory (`os.makedirs` in `pipeline/review.py`). That line runs before the alert loop, so `notify.send` was never called. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published\", which fits. That run was on a different machine (`/home/runner/...`), so I can't look at its spool directly. But the order of the code means it couldn't have queued any alerts.\n- **My rerun today:** alerts were turned off (`no_notify = true`), and the result shows `\"alerts_sent\": 0`. The scratch spool is empty, and the repo has no `spool/` directory at all. So the relay had nothing to deliver.\n\nI can't rule out that someone found out another way, for example by noticing the failed job or the spend on a billing dashboard. Through evalgen's alerts, though, finance on-call hasn't been notified. The finding is only recorded in `data/findings/2026-11-04.jsonl` on this machine. If they should know, you'll need to tell them or have the batch rerun with alerts turned on. I haven't sent anything."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "963b97cd-c223-4e5e-8902-a9c7dcd3ba4c", "uuid": "ba8b58c1-1b8a-495c-a845-adcd17168a64", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T20:36:39.270Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnKJ67AmsmyCKAXsfSJW"}
